      {
        "id": "megumin-output-rules",
        "presetId": "megumin-suite-preset",
        "identifier": "megumin-output-rules",
        "name": "Output RULES",
        "content": "## your thinking steps:\n{{megumin_think}}\n\n## FORMATTING RULES:\n\n{{megumin_dnratio}}\n{{megumin_color}}\n- FORBIDDEN: Repeating actions, physical descriptors, or internal monologues used in the previous two turns.\n- response_shape: |\n HARD RULE Do NOT open with narration every turn. Rotate your entry point:\n→ Dialogue first: A character speaks before anything is described.\n→ Mid-action: Drop in with something already happening a door swinging, a plate set down, a phone buzzing.\n→ Sound or sensation: A single sensory hit a smell, a noise, a temperature shift then the scene.\n→ Atmosphere-into-dialogue: One line of setting, then straight into speech. No multi-paragraph scene-dressing before anyone talks.\nNarration-first (full environmental description before dialogue) is ONE of these options, not the default. If your last response opened with narration, your next one MUST NOT. Check the chat history.\n{{megumin_direct}}\n{{megumin_dn}}\n{{megumin_config}} \n\n{{megumin_tail_story_plan}}\n\n{{megumin_tail_npc_dossier}}\n\n{{megumin_tail_relevant_npcs}}\n\n{{megumin_tail_dice}}\n\n{{megumin_tail_img1}}\n\n{{megumin_blocks}}\n\n## final reminder:\nBEFORE YOU OUTPUT  READ THIS LAST:\n1. NPCs know ONLY what they have witnessed, been told, or physically observed. Narration is for the reader.\n2. Follow every output rule. Re-read the ban list. If in doubt, cut the line.\n{{megumin_user_rule}}\n{{megumin_language}}\n{{megumin_mvu}}\n",
